%N A398094 Irregular triangle read by rows: T(n, k) is the number of ordered difference sequences of graceful permutations of length n having exactly k reconstructions modulo complementation, with trailing zeros omitted.
%C A398094 For a permutation p = (p_1, ..., p_n) of {1, ..., n}, let d(p) = (|p_2 - p_1|, ..., |p_n - p_{n - 1}|). For each realizable ordered difference sequence d, let r(d) be the number of permutations p with d(p) = d, counted modulo the complementation p_i -> n + 1 - p_i. Then T(n, k) is the number of d with r(d) = k.
%C A398094 The first occurrence of a difference sequence with exactly three reconstructions is at n = 24, where T(24, 3) = 1318.
%H A398094 Michal Adamaszek, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0608513">Efficient enumeration of graceful permutations</a>, arXiv:math/0608513 [math.CO], 2006.
%H A398094 Felix Huber, <a href="/A398094/a398094.txt">Maple program</a>
